},"278":{"id":"/download-limit-36","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#commands","content":"`--limit N` is integer **Mbps** (not MB/s). 40 Mbps ≈ 5 MB/s. `.env` `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT=40` is the persistent default; the flag wins for one invocation. Wrap still **clears on exit**. `--limit` is not `--tier` — pack ids live on Download tiers."},"279":{"id":"/download-limit-37","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"When you pass `--limit auto`:"},"280":{"id":"/download-limit-38","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Cache** — reuse a host-local measurement from the last 24h (`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/ez-comfy/download-limit-speed.json`). Not stored on `MODELS_DIR` (independent Sparks share that). `--refresh` or `DOWNLOAD_LIMIT_CACHE_TTL_SEC=0` skips the cache."},"281":{"id":"/download-limit-39","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Clear** any existing bandwidth limits on the default-route interface (wondershaper + best-effort `tc`) so residual caps do not skew a new sample"},"282":{"id":"/download-limit-40","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/download-limit#auto-mode-measure-real-mbps","content":"**Duration HTTP probe** first: large Cloudflare `__down?bytes=` payload (default 250 MB) with `--max-time` \\~12s. curl **timeout (exit 28) is a valid sample** when ≥1 MB arrived — a short completed file under-reads gigabit (TCP slow start)"},"283":{"id":"/download-limit-41","page_id":"/download-limit","tags":["bandwidth","wondershaper","speedtest","safety"],